{"id":"15a329b1-b044-43de-8dca-d1885257fd9b","object":"chat.completion","created":1793258810,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Baseline is recorded; phase is edit. Applying the three scoped changes now.\n\n```python\nr = replace_text(\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n'''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n''',\n'''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n\n\ndef _optional_int_min(v: str | None, minimum: int) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Parse an optional integer, enforcing a lower bound when it is set.\"\"\"\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < minimum:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{value!r} must be >= {minimum}\")\n    return value\n''', \"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\")\nprint(r['file_hash'])\n\nr2 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n'''    DEEPINFER_COMPUTE_SUM_SMALLER_PROBS = EnvVar.bool()\n    DEEPINFER_JIT_CACHE_DIR = EnvVar.str_or_none()\n''',\n'''    DEEPINFER_COMPUTE_SUM_SMALLER_PROBS = EnvVar.bool()\n    DEEPINFER_JIT_CACHE_DIR = EnvVar.str_or_none()\n\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(lambda v: _optional_int_min(v, 32))\n    \"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数；未设置表示不限长，有效值须不小于 32。\"\n''', r['file_hash'])\nprint(r2['file_hash'])\n```","reasoning_content":"Baseline pytest is marked \"doing\" but progress says baseline_done 1. So baseline likely completed. Phase=edit. Let me update plan and start editing. But I need full reading of required files — progress says reads done (Read three required source files done). However I need more of environ.py beyond line 132? The required full read is already done per plan. I have evidence for descriptor class full, rearm/rearm_all, envs class start. Need the rest of envs class and logging section maybe. Also need stats_logger full _log_worker and surroundings. I have that evidence.\n\nLet me now make edits. Budget requests left 4. Be efficient: do edits in one block with multiple replace_text calls, then run pytest.\n\nFirst, environ: add helper for max message chars and config item. Requirements: property value None when unset; else int parse, >=32, else ValueError containing var name. The descriptor wraps exception with name already (`f\"{self.name}: {e}\"`). But it says error text must contain var name; wrapping handles it. Yet for empty string int('') raises ValueError which gets wrapped with name. Good.\n\nAdd to envs: DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars) or use factory. Simpler: EnvVar(lambda v: _max_message_chars(v)). Keep within class. I'll add a module helper `_optional_int_min` maybe. But task says \"可增加必要标准库辅助函数\". I'll add helper:\n\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{v!r}, must be >= 32\")\n    return value\n\nWrapped by descriptor gives DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS prefix.\n\nWhere to add? Add to envs class under a new \"-- Logging --\" section. Preserve existing.\n\nLogger: extend NewLineFormatter __init__ with keyword-only max_message_chars. Signature currently four positional params. Add `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None`. Validate: bool excluded; int >=32 else ValueError. Store truncated marker.\n\nformat: need message body truncation after args substitution, without mutating record. Approach: call a helper that formats message with record.args but not prefix. Could do:\n\nmsg_body = record.getMessage()  # does %-substitution, doesn't mutate\nBut record.message is set by super().format(record). Plan: first handle budget on a shallow copy? Requirement: \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" and \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\". Easiest: compute truncated message before calling super().format, by creating a copy of the record? But super().format sets record.message and formats exception. We can compute:\n\nbody = record.getMessage()\nif not keep_full and max is not None and len(body) > max:\n    body = truncate(body)\n    record = copy.copy(record)\n    record.msg = body\n    record.args = None\n    # clear exc_info/stack_info? Requirement says don't mutate originals; copy can clear them to avoid duplicating traceback? Actually keep exception handling same. Hmm. If record had exc_info, super().format appends traceback. We shouldn't truncate traceback. Keeping exc_info on copy is fine — message replaced, traceback still appended. stack_info also.\nThen msg = super().format(record) — but record.message accessed later for newline prefix. On copy, record.message is truncated body. Good.\n\nBut careful: `record.getMessage()` may itself raise for weird args; super().format handles gracefully. Fine.\n\nAlso \"预算只限制消息正文，不包含... 异常回溯或 stack_info\". Using body replacement keeps those.\n\nkeep_full check: `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True`.\n\nTruncation:\nTRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\nremaining = max - len(marker)\nhead = (remaining + 1) // 2\ntail = remaining - head\nbody = body[:head] + marker + body[-tail:] if tail else body[:head] + marker\n\nFor budget 32: remaining=17, head=9, tail=8. Good.\n\nEdge: max >=32 ensures remaining >=17 positive.\n\nThen in format, after super().format maybe record.message for prefix. Using copy works.\n\nNeed import copy.\n\n_setup_logger: read envs config. logger.py imports os already. Need `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Any circular import? environ imports only stdlib. Fine. But logger is imported early; environ independent. Add import guard? Direct import.\n\nmax_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS.\n\nNote `_setup_logger()` at import; unset default None.\n\nstats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nAlso ensure default handler not duplicated: existing.\n\nNow I need the exact text for replace edits.